  "summary_en": "Arizona's 2018 act (HB 2422) defines personal delivery devices (sidewalk delivery robots under 100 lb, up to 10 mph) and permits their operation on sidewalks and crosswalks. It sets pedestrian-like rights, identification plates, braking, operator monitoring, a $100,000 insurance requirement, local restrictions, and civil penalties, and exempts the devices from vehicle registration.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Defines personal delivery device (under 100 lb, max 10 mph) and operator; excluded from 'motor vehicle' and 'vehicle'.",
   "Devices may operate on sidewalks/crosswalks with pedestrian rights and duties, must yield to pedestrians.",
   "Requires ID plate with operator contact info and a braking system; operator must actively control or monitor.",
   "Operating entity must carry at least $100,000 general liability insurance.",
   "Civil penalty up to $500 per violation; local authorities may adopt reasonable restrictions; exempt from registration and financial responsibility."
  ],
